\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {4}{\ignorespaces Where the acquisition budget is spent, projected to two dimensions with t-SNE, for one ImageNet-100-LT run. Grey marks scores below the 75th percentile, blue the q75--q99 acquisition band, and red the anchors farthest-point sampling selects from that band. The band occupies the periphery of the projection: over the panel shown, the rank correlation between $k$NN score and distance from the projection centre is $+0.51$, and band members sit at mean radius 34.6 against 25.5 for the rest. The anchors are spread across the band and not clustered inside it, which is the behaviour farthest-point sampling is included to produce. Each panel is projected separately because the encoder changes between cycles, so positions are comparable within a panel and not across panels. The panel contains original images only, so it shows which regions are targeted and not what the inserted samples do to them; Table~\ref {tab:fixed-support} measures the latter directly.}}{16}{figure.caption.28}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:cycle-tsne}{{4}{16}{Where the acquisition budget is spent, projected to two dimensions with t-SNE, for one ImageNet-100-LT run. Grey marks scores below the 75th percentile, blue the q75--q99 acquisition band, and red the anchors farthest-point sampling selects from that band. The band occupies the periphery of the projection: over the panel shown, the rank correlation between $k$NN score and distance from the projection centre is $+0.51$, and band members sit at mean radius 34.6 against 25.5 for the rest. The anchors are spread across the band and not clustered inside it, which is the behaviour farthest-point sampling is included to produce. Each panel is projected separately because the encoder changes between cycles, so positions are comparable within a panel and not across panels. The panel contains original images only, so it shows which regions are targeted and not what the inserted samples do to them; Table~\ref {tab:fixed-support} measures the latter directly}{figure.caption.28}{}}
